knowledge, new viewpoint that comes from Grothendieck's theory of dessins
d'enfants and, unlike these approaches, takes into account the order in which
vertices appear in each hyperedge and hyperedges appear around each vertex. A
dessin is a bipartite graph drawn on a closed orientable surface. Through
Walsh's classical correspondence between hypermaps and bipartite maps, every
hypergraph equipped with a cyclic order of incidences at each vertex and inside
each hyperedge is a dessin, and therefore determines a surface with faces and a
